{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Rosenberg&limit=10&title=How The West Grew Rich","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"titleInfo":{"title":"How the West grew rich","subTitle":"the economic transformation of the industrial world"},"name":[{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Rosenberg, Nathan",{"@type":"date","#text":"1927-"}],"role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Birdzell, L. E. (Luther Earle)"}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History"}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"publisher":"Basic Books","dateIssued":["c1986",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"1986"}],"issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xii, 353 p. ; 25 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Rosenberg and Birdzell examine how the West--Europe, Canada, and the United States--escaped from poverty into sustained economic growth and material well-being. They present an interpretative study of the economic development of the Western world since the Middle Ages and argue that the political pluralism and flexibility of the West's institutions explain its prosperity and wealth. The authors demonstrate that the break-up of centralized political and religious controls encouraged the expansion of trade and the growth of urban culture, along with the scientific, cultural, and political freedom that was necessary to feed economic and technological innovations. ISBN 0-465-03108-0 : $19.95."},"tableOfContents":"1. Introduction -- 2. The starting point : the Middle Ages -- 3. The growth of trade to 1750 -- 4. The evolution of institutions favorable to commerce -- 5. The development of industry : 1750-1880 -- 6. Diversity of organization : the corporation -- 7. Technology, trusts, and marketable stock -- 8. The link between science and wealth -- 9. Diversity of enterprise -- 10. Implications and comparisons.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Nathan Rosenberg & L.E. Birdzell, Jr."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographies and index."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":[{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"ew-----"},{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}]},{"temporal":"Geschichte 1500-1986"},{"@authority":"swd","temporal":"Geschichte 1500-1986"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Economic history"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Capitalism","History"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":"Europe","topic":"Economic conditions"},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":"United States","topic":"Economic conditions"}],"classification":{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HC240 .R67 1986"},"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"How the West grew rich"},"name":{"namePart":"Rosenberg, Nathan, 1927-"},"originInfo":{"publisher":"New York : Basic Books, ©1986"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)654247339"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990004370750203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0465031080 :"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^85047551^//r86"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"12550347"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000463633307","#text":"Lamont Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HC240 .R67 1986"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000123374